{"name":"Depth Charge","hex":"#355859","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"depth charge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of bomb, launched from a ship or dropped from an aircraft, that is designed to detonate at a certain depth underwater for the purposes of attacking a submerged enemy, especially a submarine.","Synonym of bomb shot (“type of mixed drink”)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attack (a target, usually a submarine) with depth charges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depth_charge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Depth charge","blocks":[{"text":"A depth charge is an anti-submarine warfare (ASW) weapon designed to destroy submarines by detonating in the water near the target and subjecting it to a destructive hydraulic shock. Most depth charges use high explosives with a fuze set to detonate the charge, typically at a specific depth from the surface. Depth charges can be dropped by ships, patrol aircraft and helicopters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Depth_charge_bd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depth_charge"},{"title":"Depth Charge (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Depth Charge (1941–1965) was a Thoroughbred son of Bold Venture who went on to become an outstanding sire of American Quarter Horse racehorses. He was posthumously inducted into the AQHA Hall of Fame"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depth_Charge_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Mk-101_Lulu_NDB.jpg/500px-Mk-101_Lulu_NDB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Mk-101_Lulu_NDB.jpg/500px-Mk-101_Lulu_NDB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mk 101 Lulu was a US nuclear depth bomb operational from 1958 to 1972","link":"h